+
+This candidate changes only native-mailbox.yml, runner shell, fixture-check.sh/export-evidence.py and associated Python tests, plus these docs. App product/44Swift/33Foundation inputs/API/shared/Tools/nativeUI assertions remain unchanged. No Apple/compiler/grammar/423/API/fullBun/CI/remote/child reviewer or new test execution occurred while authoring. Original11 test method BODIES (7checkpoint and4phase) and all literal selection arrays are statically compared byte-exact; default/failfast expectations and original singleton assertions remain. The exact inventory, rather than prose, lists11 old methods.
+
+The fixed light/dark matrix has fail-fast:false, separate50m macOS jobs/45m steps and fresh existing owned fixture/simulator per job. Safe requested appearance enters identity/artifact name. The old required Native mailbox light/dark UI context is a Linux always/needs aggregate that fails for failure/cancel/skipped/no-success results. No appearance or unit suite is removed; OrcaTests remains light-only. Both default keeps old ordering/failure behavior; explicit shards only run their own adoption/main phases and report only actual selected exits/bundles. Input validation rejects malformed and nonmailbox single appearances before Xcode/fixture startup at both entry boundaries. Existing privacy/owned cleanup/per-case deadlines/appearance reset remain.
+
+Dark checkpoint is only a second fixed allowlisted phase. Same private full staging/redaction/token scan, fresh scratch and atomic publication, null/false incomplete marker, final outcome last and preservation on corrupt later export remain. An extra export consumes the same45m budget; neither synthetic work nor split design proves each real shard fits or UI passes. Known kill-before-atomic-publication gap remains. Cleanup restoration to Light is still actual simulator cleanup, not a claim that a dark-only suite executed Light tests.
+
+Planned execution after ROOT immutable review/allocation:5 actual mainphase harness methods/40 parameter invocations (36old+2originalfailure+2selectedzero),6 source-backed shard-contract methods (invalid direct/wrapper ingress5+6; real fixtureforward+identity4; actualadoption6; all selector bytes/lightunits; real aggregate statuses5 plus fixedmatrix contract),11 actual checkpoint methods (7old unchanged incl outerkill+4new dark controls),25 unchanged sanitizer methods,4 existing runner-lifecycle scopes, bash/zsh syntax. Total47 unittest METHODS, with parameter observations separately enumerated; no invented single aggregate scenario total. Original singleton assertions were not replaced. Actual phase blocks/adoption/progress/fixture-forward/identity/aggregate are extracted from production code with mock executable boundaries, not parallel implementations. Workflow structural assertions cannot by themselves prove GitHub scheduling; hosted both-appearance results remain decisive.
+
+Request one bounded~40s ROOT slot as a source estimate, not a measured speed claim. Each existing/request deadline remains unchanged. Capture compile/setup/raw stage exits, zero skips/full exactmethod completion, actual call/bundle/selected exit, source hashes and owned cleanup; preserve any partial/cap/setup failure as NONPASS. No automatic retry or publication permission. Publication remains HOLD and all724native failure/after-shot/all33 gates stay open.
